WEBVTT

01:19.872 --> 01:20.873
It's...

01:22.708 --> 01:24.710
Yeah. This way.

01:27.462 --> 01:29.464
Okay. Okay.

01:31.550 --> 01:34.135
Here we are inside
something called Agri-Jet.

01:34.136 --> 01:39.599
It's a refrigerated warehouse in
Albuquerque, New Mexico.

01:39.600 --> 01:40.767
Jesus.

01:41.476 --> 01:43.312
It's cold in here.

01:44.313 --> 01:47.648
All right, let me show you around.
I'll give you a sense of the place,

01:47.649 --> 01:49.358
give you the grand tour.

01:49.359 --> 01:51.110
It's... It's huge.

01:51.111 --> 01:52.946
It's maybe hundred feet long.

01:53.614 --> 01:55.948
I don't know what that is in meters,
but it's massive.

01:55.949 --> 01:58.452
And it is packed to the rafters

01:58.994 --> 02:03.248
with lots and lots of...

02:04.208 --> 02:05.792
shrink-wrapped...

02:07.252 --> 02:08.252
items.

02:10.005 --> 02:12.341
Yeah, so what's inside?

02:13.258 --> 02:14.301
Well...

02:15.552 --> 02:17.386
A picture's worth a thousand words, right?

02:17.387 --> 02:19.681
So, I'm gonna let you see for yourself.

02:23.393 --> 02:24.478
Okay.

02:29.066 --> 02:30.067
Okay.

02:30.901 --> 02:32.318
Do you see this?

02:32.319 --> 02:34.196
Huh? Yeah.

02:34.905 --> 02:35.906
It's...

02:36.990 --> 02:39.075
That is not a Butterball turkey.

02:39.076 --> 02:40.494
I'll tell you that much.

02:41.411 --> 02:43.120
What are they doing with all this, huh?

02:43.121 --> 02:44.455
Guess.

02:44.456 --> 02:46.123
Fucking guess.

02:46.124 --> 02:50.962
Because this whole place is filled

02:50.963 --> 02:52.464
with human bodies.

02:53.090 --> 02:54.549
It's parts of them!

02:54.550 --> 02:56.717
It's pieces of them.

02:56.718 --> 02:59.638
All vacuum sealed.

03:00.973 --> 03:04.476
That is what this whole plant
is being used for.

03:06.353 --> 03:08.437
And it's been happening
right under our noses.

03:08.438 --> 03:11.233
I mean, they got out
of this town in a hurry,

03:12.401 --> 03:14.069
but I guarantee you, before that,

03:14.736 --> 03:17.072
they were probably doing
three shifts a day in here.

03:18.574 --> 03:21.076
And what's behind that door, huh?

03:23.161 --> 03:27.498
It is a meat grinder
the size of a bus and vats,

03:27.499 --> 03:29.333
cooking vats.

03:29.334 --> 03:31.503
And wait until you see
what's inside those.

07:58.645 --> 08:02.357
Two million, four hundred thousand even.

08:43.273 --> 08:44.274
All in.

08:49.446 --> 08:51.448
All in.

09:00.290 --> 09:02.250
Five million dollars.

09:02.251 --> 09:04.336
The house record.

09:19.142 --> 09:20.561
Are you sure?

09:36.743 --> 09:38.453
Please reveal your cards.

09:45.419 --> 09:46.712
A straight flush.

10:12.905 --> 10:14.531
A royal flush.

10:15.073 --> 10:16.450
The higher hand.

10:30.714 --> 10:33.175
Hey, pal. Stay in character.

10:38.931 --> 10:42.059
You may have won this time, Mr. Diabaté.

10:42.935 --> 10:44.937
But your luck is about to run out.

10:46.021 --> 10:47.648
Someday, perhaps...

10:52.653 --> 10:54.655
but not today.

10:55.572 --> 10:57.074
For you, my lovely.

10:59.576 --> 11:01.161
It's been an honor.

11:10.087 --> 11:11.255
Anyone else?

11:14.800 --> 11:18.637
Come, my beauties.

11:27.271 --> 11:28.397
Next time.

11:31.233 --> 11:32.985
It's been a pleasure!

12:43.931 --> 12:45.431
And you are?

12:45.432 --> 12:48.309
- Joette.
- Joette!

12:48.310 --> 12:51.063
Come in, my dear.

13:05.869 --> 13:08.287
We're terribly sorry, our love,

13:08.288 --> 13:11.124
but we have to leave immediately.

13:11.834 --> 13:13.627
What? Why?

13:13.836 --> 13:16.046
You're going to have a visitor.

13:20.968 --> 13:24.721
You can come with us, if you want.

13:26.640 --> 13:29.267
I can't do that to her.

13:29.268 --> 13:31.812
Sooner or later, we'll have to talk.

13:34.982 --> 13:37.526
Is there no time for even a little...?

13:40.612 --> 13:41.613
Joette?

14:01.049 --> 14:03.676
Please be here.
Please be here. Please be here.

14:03.677 --> 14:05.596
Please be here. Please be here.

15:56.290 --> 15:57.457
Hello?

16:16.435 --> 16:17.603
In here.

16:29.031 --> 16:31.200
Just in time, Carol.

16:32.034 --> 16:36.622
So, on their way out the door,
they told you I was coming?

16:38.790 --> 16:40.792
- Why'd you stay?
- To welcome you.

16:42.169 --> 16:43.419
No, thanks.

16:43.420 --> 16:44.671
I appreciate that.

16:47.174 --> 16:49.176
I bet they didn't tell you
why I was coming.

16:49.718 --> 16:51.553
There's no way in hell they did.

16:52.804 --> 16:54.514
You're gonna need something
stronger than champagne

16:54.515 --> 16:55.974
when you see what I brought.

16:56.600 --> 16:57.768
Do you...

17:00.020 --> 17:02.523
have a TV in this barn?

17:10.739 --> 17:11.740
Impressive.

17:22.584 --> 17:23.585
Okay.

17:24.336 --> 17:27.338
What do you got? H... HDMI. All right.

17:27.339 --> 17:29.757
Is this another one of your videos?

17:29.758 --> 17:30.926
You've seen my videos?

17:33.428 --> 17:35.096
They actually sent you my videos?

17:35.097 --> 17:36.180
Of course.

17:36.181 --> 17:37.516
They were very well done.

17:38.308 --> 17:39.476
Very dramatic.

17:40.811 --> 17:42.813
Well, you could have...

17:44.898 --> 17:46.274
Forget it.

17:46.275 --> 17:47.568
When you see this one...

17:49.945 --> 17:51.029
Let's just say...

17:52.364 --> 17:53.615
It's disturbing.

17:54.199 --> 17:56.576
And I hate to use a cliché,

17:56.577 --> 17:58.996
but you might want to sit down. Seriously.

17:59.705 --> 18:01.789
'Cause I am telling you
what you are about to witness--

18:01.790 --> 18:03.584
Is this about them eating people?

18:06.253 --> 18:08.255
- What?
- It is troubling.

18:09.798 --> 18:11.800
Wait, how would you... How could you...

18:12.718 --> 18:13.802
Allow me.

18:17.848 --> 18:19.682
Hello, Carol. We're John Cena,

18:19.683 --> 18:22.435
and we're here to address some questions
you may be having

18:22.436 --> 18:23.854
regarding our food supply.

18:25.439 --> 18:27.690
As you know,
we can't purposely kill, harm,

18:27.691 --> 18:30.277
or otherwise interfere
with any form of life.

18:31.153 --> 18:33.155
That limits what we're able to consume.

18:33.780 --> 18:37.033
Because when we say "any life,"
that includes plant life.

18:37.034 --> 18:39.869
We can't harvest wheat or corn or rice.

18:39.870 --> 18:41.788
We can't pluck an apple from a tree.

18:42.372 --> 18:44.123
Once an apple drops of its own accord,

18:44.124 --> 18:46.418
well, we'll eat it, of course,
and gratefully.

18:47.044 --> 18:49.629
Indeed, we harvest
all the windfall we can find.

18:49.630 --> 18:51.965
Plus, there are billions
of domesticated animals,

18:52.549 --> 18:55.761
cows, chief amongst them,
that still require milking.

18:56.345 --> 18:59.680
And there's preexisting food,
millions of tons of it,

18:59.681 --> 19:01.767
that was processed prior to our joining.

19:02.518 --> 19:03.936
So far, so good, right?

19:04.937 --> 19:06.647
Except for one small problem.

19:07.231 --> 19:14.154
As of this taping,
there are 7,348,292,411 of us.

19:14.905 --> 19:16.657
That's a lot of mouths to feed.

19:17.366 --> 19:18.951
We're facing a caloric deficit,

19:19.451 --> 19:22.204
and to make up for it,
we've had to take certain measures.

19:23.622 --> 19:26.123
This is how we get our sustenance.

19:26.124 --> 19:29.920
One half-pint of this shelf-stable liquid
contains 300 calories.

19:30.546 --> 19:34.006
Which means that based on
a diet of 2,400 calories a day,

19:34.007 --> 19:38.427
someone John Cena's size
needs eight of these every 24 hours.

19:38.428 --> 19:42.015
Larger individuals require more.
Smaller ones, less.

19:42.808 --> 19:43.975
What's in it?

19:43.976 --> 19:45.560
Well, a lot of things.

19:45.561 --> 19:47.436
It's manufactured across the globe,

19:47.437 --> 19:51.191
so the recipe changes based on
the local availability of ingredients.

19:51.775 --> 19:54.944
Mostly, it's those stockpiled
foodstuffs we spoke of,

19:54.945 --> 19:57.447
particularly ones that
are in danger of spoiling.

19:58.240 --> 20:01.325
Additionally, each carton
contains eight to 12%

20:01.326 --> 20:03.161
of something we call HDP.

20:03.704 --> 20:05.204
Human-derived protein.

20:05.205 --> 20:07.583
And yep,
that's pretty much what it sounds like.

20:08.417 --> 20:13.337
Nearly 100,000 people pass away each day
due to natural causes and accidents.

20:13.338 --> 20:16.007
Those human remains,
which would otherwise go to waste,

20:16.008 --> 20:17.843
are our source of HDP.

20:18.677 --> 20:22.431
We cherish the memory of these people
and appreciate their sacrifice.

20:23.015 --> 20:26.101
Given our druthers,
would we choose to consume HDP?

20:26.894 --> 20:28.019
No.

20:28.020 --> 20:30.730
Throughout history, most cultures,
though not all,

20:30.731 --> 20:32.900
have taken a dim view of anthropophagy.

20:33.525 --> 20:36.445
Honestly, we're not
that keen on it ourselves.

20:37.112 --> 20:38.864
But we're left with little choice.

20:39.656 --> 20:42.700
Rest assured, Carol, you will
never have to consume this product.

20:42.701 --> 20:46.120
Not unless you want to,
which we assume is unlikely.

20:46.121 --> 20:50.208
We will never serve HDP to you
in any form at any time.

20:50.209 --> 20:52.460
We will continue
to reserve only the freshest,

20:52.461 --> 20:55.130
best windfall
and stockpiled foods for you.

20:55.756 --> 20:57.840
We hope that clears things up.

20:57.841 --> 21:01.762
As always, your well-being is
of the utmost importance to us.

21:02.262 --> 21:06.350
Any comments, concerns, call any
time, day or night, and leave a voicemail.

21:07.309 --> 21:09.685
We regret not being able
to speak to you directly,

21:09.686 --> 21:12.189
but for the time being, we need our space.

21:19.530 --> 21:21.031
So you knew all about this?

21:21.907 --> 21:23.492
How... When...

21:24.201 --> 21:25.243
For how long?

21:25.244 --> 21:28.956
About a week ago, out of curiosity,
I asked John Cena,

21:29.665 --> 21:31.667
"Why do you people drink so much milk?"

21:32.209 --> 21:33.627
We had been hanging out together.

21:34.169 --> 21:36.755
He was teaching me
the sunset flip powerbomb.

21:37.506 --> 21:39.382
And what was your reaction?

21:39.383 --> 21:40.716
Do you even have one?

21:40.717 --> 21:42.469
As I said, it is troubling.

21:43.637 --> 21:44.888
Very much so.

21:45.639 --> 21:47.975
It probably helps that
I've had time to think about it.

21:48.851 --> 21:51.936
I must say John Cena makes
a fairly reasonable case.

21:51.937 --> 21:53.729
In French, he's even more convincing.

21:53.730 --> 21:56.817
That is not John Cena.

21:57.651 --> 22:00.487
Jesus Christ, why are you so...

22:02.322 --> 22:06.158
How about the fact that in Spain
they all said they were vegetarians?

22:06.159 --> 22:08.245
Yes, I asked John about that.

22:08.745 --> 22:10.746
He reminded me that
technically what they said was

22:10.747 --> 22:13.416
that they would prefer to be vegetarian.

22:13.417 --> 22:16.627
Oh, great, so all the fucking
lawyers in the world survived.

22:16.628 --> 22:18.087
Carol, for the record,

22:18.088 --> 22:22.175
I am in no way pleased with the idea
of these people eating human flesh.

22:22.176 --> 22:23.801
None of us are.

22:23.802 --> 22:24.887
Us?

22:26.638 --> 22:27.723
Who's us?

22:32.269 --> 22:33.604
The other individuals.

22:35.063 --> 22:36.899
The ones like you and me.

22:38.442 --> 22:39.443
We stay in touch.

22:42.196 --> 22:43.197
You stay in touch?

22:44.114 --> 22:45.114
All 12 of you?

22:45.115 --> 22:47.533
All but one.
There's a gentleman in Paraguay.

22:47.534 --> 22:50.621
Chaperones reach out,
but he doesn't reply.

22:51.455 --> 22:54.540
But the other 11 of us, yes.

22:54.541 --> 22:56.293
So the 11 of you, you...

22:57.461 --> 23:00.047
What? You just hang out?

23:01.590 --> 23:03.508
Potluck suppers and whatnot.

23:03.509 --> 23:05.218
- We meet occasionally.
- Okay.

23:05.219 --> 23:07.094
Tuesdays and Fridays.

23:07.095 --> 23:08.638
Oh, well, that's a lot of flying.

23:08.639 --> 23:10.140
Mostly, we're on Zoom.

23:12.768 --> 23:13.852
Right.

23:14.853 --> 23:16.188
What do you guys talk about?

23:17.064 --> 23:20.066
I mean, it can't be saving the world
'cause you shot that down really quickly.

23:20.067 --> 23:22.026
In a sense it is.

23:22.027 --> 23:27.783
Carol, what John Cena did not mention
is that even with the HDP,

23:28.784 --> 23:32.787
most of the world's population will
starve to death within the next ten years.

23:32.788 --> 23:34.623
- Says who?
- Says them.

23:35.707 --> 23:37.376
If you press them long enough.

23:38.168 --> 23:40.587
We wish to save them from that.

23:41.255 --> 23:44.424
At our most recent gathering,
we pitched the idea of robotic farming.

23:45.092 --> 23:48.345
However, as it is, they would have
to build and program the robots.

23:50.097 --> 23:51.597
They did appreciate the input.

23:51.598 --> 23:52.683
I bet.

23:54.309 --> 23:58.313
Did you guys ever talk about
including me in the Zooms?

23:59.606 --> 24:00.607
I mean...

24:02.651 --> 24:04.735
I am a professional writer,
and no offense,

24:04.736 --> 24:07.656
but I can come up with shit
like robots all day long.

24:08.240 --> 24:09.491
We...

24:10.367 --> 24:11.618
We took a vote.

24:12.286 --> 24:13.703
It was not unanimous,

24:13.704 --> 24:17.207
but the majority felt
your presence might prove...

24:19.084 --> 24:20.169
disruptive.

24:23.172 --> 24:25.673
Also, our non-English speakers
were perhaps a bit offended that

24:25.674 --> 24:28.218
you did not invite them
to join us in Spain.

24:30.179 --> 24:31.929
I'm sorry, Carol.

24:31.930 --> 24:34.433
Ultimately this is not about you.

24:35.100 --> 24:37.518
Or any of us, for that matter.

24:37.519 --> 24:38.937
Yeah, sure. I get it.

24:42.357 --> 24:43.942
Where's your nearest bathroom?

25:22.147 --> 25:25.234
But she's so lonely.

25:26.944 --> 25:29.112
Yes, I know.

25:30.697 --> 25:31.782
Okay.

25:36.578 --> 25:39.164
I miss you too, my loves.

25:40.290 --> 25:42.626
See you soon.

27:16.053 --> 27:17.137
You're awake.

27:17.763 --> 27:20.599
Once again, your timing is perfect.

27:21.725 --> 27:22.893
Please, sit.

27:38.951 --> 27:40.953
That looks good. Thanks.

28:49.354 --> 28:50.355
So...

28:51.315 --> 28:52.773
what are your plans?

28:52.774 --> 28:56.612
Well, I'm sure you need a break from me.

28:59.698 --> 29:01.782
I have enjoyed your company, Carol.

29:01.783 --> 29:03.618
- You like your space. I get it.
- No.

29:03.619 --> 29:07.872
So, I was thinking
I'll go find my own suite,

29:07.873 --> 29:09.791
get cleaned up, and then,

29:10.751 --> 29:12.169
we can get together later.

29:12.711 --> 29:13.962
Talk some more.

29:26.808 --> 29:28.101
I'm just messing with you.

29:33.941 --> 29:35.316
Well done.

29:35.317 --> 29:37.986
Truth is,
I can't get out of Vegas fast enough.

29:38.529 --> 29:42.699
This city is like
a trillion dollar light-up ashtray.

29:44.326 --> 29:46.327
No offense to your new town.

29:46.328 --> 29:48.163
No, none taken.

29:48.830 --> 29:50.582
I'm sure it's no Albuquerque.

29:54.336 --> 29:56.337
Carol, you can always call me.

29:56.338 --> 29:59.007
Dial zero,
and they will find me wherever I am.

29:59.842 --> 30:00.926
Thanks.

30:01.468 --> 30:02.553
How you say,

30:03.303 --> 30:05.137
"check in" now and then, hmm?

30:05.138 --> 30:06.390
Sure.

30:08.058 --> 30:11.478
Maybe you will have some ideas on how
to save these people from starvation.

30:13.522 --> 30:14.523
I don't know.

30:15.065 --> 30:17.484
Maybe tell 'em to pick a fucking apple.

30:18.402 --> 30:20.153
- Wow.
- Sorry.

30:20.779 --> 30:21.864
I didn't mean that.

30:23.031 --> 30:24.700
I mean, fuck it, yes, I did.

30:25.284 --> 30:26.535
I meant that, but...

30:27.744 --> 30:28.912
not like it sounded.

30:29.830 --> 30:32.624
I'm not some kind of monster, you know?

30:33.166 --> 30:34.251
I just...

30:34.918 --> 30:36.335
They're doing this to themselves.

30:36.336 --> 30:38.421
They are choosing to starve.

30:38.422 --> 30:40.756
- They do not see it that way.
- Listen to me.

30:40.757 --> 30:45.094
The only way to save these lunatics
is to turn them back the way they were.

30:45.095 --> 30:48.389
There is a way to reverse this.

30:48.390 --> 30:49.975
Help me find it.

30:50.601 --> 30:53.603
Do you seriously think
the world is a better place now,

30:53.604 --> 30:55.105
just because it's peaceful?

30:57.316 --> 31:01.068
Well, once they turn us,
we're gonna starve right along with them.

31:01.069 --> 31:02.738
Have you thought of that?

31:04.114 --> 31:05.616
They cannot turn us,

31:06.825 --> 31:08.493
not without our consent.

31:12.706 --> 31:13.749
What do you mean?

31:14.249 --> 31:16.542
It seems the only way
to make their virus work on us

31:16.543 --> 31:19.879
is by tailoring it
to our individual stem cells.

31:19.880 --> 31:23.634
But to obtain those stem cells, they
must first collect them from our bodies.

31:24.801 --> 31:25.885
What... What?

31:25.886 --> 31:29.973
Apparently that involves sticking
a large needle into the bone of the hip.

31:30.807 --> 31:32.308
Somewhat painful.

31:32.309 --> 31:33.685
And very invasive.

31:35.354 --> 31:38.440
Something they cannot do
without our permission.

31:40.984 --> 31:42.402
When did you find this out?

31:43.070 --> 31:45.072
They made this discovery only yesterday.

31:45.906 --> 31:48.242
They are not pleased about it,
I can assure you.

31:50.118 --> 31:52.120
They asked me if I would give my consent.

31:53.163 --> 31:54.331
I said,

31:55.123 --> 31:58.877
"Regrettably, as of this time,
I prefer not to."

32:12.015 --> 32:13.599
Hello, Carol.

32:13.600 --> 32:14.935
This is a recording.

32:15.644 --> 32:19.897
At the tone, you can leave a message
to request anything you might need.

32:19.898 --> 32:21.650
We'll do our best to provide it.

32:22.359 --> 32:24.987
Our feelings for you
haven't changed, Carol.

32:25.571 --> 32:29.408
But after everything that's happened,
we just need a little space.

32:32.369 --> 32:33.453
It's me.

32:34.413 --> 32:38.916
Is it true that you need
our stem cells to turn us into you?

32:38.917 --> 32:42.336
And furthermore, is it true that
you need our express permission

32:42.337 --> 32:44.923
to collect those stem cells?

32:57.436 --> 32:58.520
Carol.

33:25.672 --> 33:27.256
Hello, Carol.

33:27.257 --> 33:28.509
This is a recording.

33:29.259 --> 33:33.429
At the tone, you can leave a message
to request anything you might need.

33:33.430 --> 33:35.307
We'll do our best to provide it.

33:35.891 --> 33:38.893
Our feelings for you
haven't changed, Carol.

33:38.894 --> 33:42.773
But after everything that's happened,
we just need a little space.

33:44.942 --> 33:50.530
I am officially going on record
that I do not consent.

33:50.531 --> 33:52.783
You will not lay a finger on me.

33:53.951 --> 33:55.369
Repeat that back.

34:36.076 --> 34:37.828
This is your vehicle?

34:38.411 --> 34:39.413
Yep.

34:42.748 --> 34:44.168
Interesting choice.

34:47.462 --> 34:48.463
You too.

35:07.649 --> 35:11.236
For what it's worth,
the world is doing the best it can.

35:11.987 --> 35:13.071
It misses you.

35:13.697 --> 35:15.199
Zosia misses you.

35:15.782 --> 35:17.201
They want to come back, Carol.

35:18.035 --> 35:20.913
They're just looking
for a change of heart.

35:22.372 --> 35:23.373
Fuck 'em.

35:25.542 --> 35:26.710
Watch your toes.

39:58.315 --> 40:00.483
To my 12 fellow survivors...

40:00.484 --> 40:01.567
Twelve?

40:01.568 --> 40:03.654
...greetings. I'm Carol Sturka.

40:04.446 --> 40:05.738
Some of you know me.

40:05.739 --> 40:07.324
Some of you I've yet to meet.

40:07.824 --> 40:11.245
But... if you're still one of us,

40:12.454 --> 40:13.956
then this message is for you.

40:16.875 --> 40:19.461
There is a way to undo this situation.

40:20.212 --> 40:23.632
To turn the world back
the way it's supposed to be.

40:26.260 --> 40:27.593
How do I know this?

40:27.594 --> 40:33.683
Because earlier today,
these afflicted people, these Others,

40:33.684 --> 40:35.435
they basically told me so themselves.

40:36.311 --> 40:37.396
Because guess what?

40:38.105 --> 40:40.107
They can't lie.

40:41.316 --> 40:43.526
Which is yet another thing
I've discovered.

40:43.527 --> 40:47.154
This alien virus or whatever it is,

40:47.155 --> 40:50.576
it doesn't allow them to do that.

40:51.410 --> 40:55.831
So, what is this solution exactly?

40:56.707 --> 40:58.124
That they didn't tell me.

40:58.125 --> 41:01.461
But they so resisted telling me,

41:02.254 --> 41:04.798
that everybody suddenly burst into tears.

41:05.382 --> 41:08.177
Worldwide, apparently.

41:08.802 --> 41:10.637
Which I know upset at least one of you.

41:11.346 --> 41:12.930
And then after that,

41:12.931 --> 41:16.435
they completely abandoned
the city I live in.

41:17.352 --> 41:19.771
Leaving me here all alone.

41:20.355 --> 41:22.774
Which says to me I'm on the right track.

41:24.109 --> 41:28.197
Now, I realize some of you

41:28.989 --> 41:31.575
think the world
might be better off this way,

41:32.451 --> 41:35.454
with all the newfound peace,
love and understanding.

41:36.747 --> 41:37.915
Enjoy that opinion.

41:39.208 --> 41:40.417
Relish it.

41:41.084 --> 41:43.504
Because it may be
the last one you ever possess.

41:44.129 --> 41:48.466
And when the day comes that you have
peace and love forced upon you,

41:48.467 --> 41:51.220
who knows,
maybe in that last fleeting moment,

41:52.137 --> 41:56.141
you might just realize
you treasure your individuality.

43:32.112 --> 43:34.781
If there is someone here,
I advise you to get out now.

46:33.168 --> 46:34.711
Hello, son.

46:42.511 --> 46:44.471
We're happy to see you.

46:47.683 --> 46:50.811
You must be hungry and confused.

46:54.565 --> 46:56.984
Can we answer any questions?

47:05.993 --> 47:09.496
Tell us. What can we do for you, son?

47:12.958 --> 47:15.002
Don't call me son. You're not my mother.

47:20.048 --> 47:22.092
My mother's a bitch.
